.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_RAW_CHUNK_SIZE_GET 3 2026-11-03 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_raw_chunk_size_get \- query patch writer raw-MD5 chunk size
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_raw_chunk_size_get("
.BI "        mpq_patch_s *" "patch,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "raw_chunk_size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Return the patch writer's configured raw-chunk size without changing its
state or locking configuration. The v4 default is 0x4000 (16 KiB); zero
means trailing raw-MD5 arrays are disabled. Older generations return zero.
The getter remains usable after member writing or signing locks setters,
while the patch handle remains valid. Finish and abort consume that handle.
.PP
This reports physical raw policy, not checksum availability or verification
success. It does not expose the private archive or configure a transaction.
A valid output pointer is cleared before validation. A latched terminal
writer error is returned unchanged, with the output left zero.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success or a negative libmpq error code.
The output is cleared on failure when its pointer is valid.
.SH ERRORS
Missing required pointers return LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. Terminal writer errors
are returned unchanged. Failed queries leave a valid output pointer zero.
